      "check": "balance",
      "difference": 1,
      "source_page": 9,
      "note": "Statement of revenues, expenditures and changes in fund balances prints ending fund balance 9,011,016 (General 8,101,166) (p9), while the governmental funds balance sheet prints total fund balances 9,011,015 (General 8,101,165) (pp6-7); rounding in the report."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Modified cash basis city, FY ended 9/30/2022. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (pp8-9), Total Governmental Funds column; transfers in 567,218 is the Total column after the Eliminations column (General out 613,015 to Debt Service eliminated). Fund balances recorded as fund balances (beginning 8,936,080, ending 9,011,016, p9); beginning cash not printed; ending_cash = sum of the four cash lines of the governmental funds statement of assets (p5), as in FY2023. Identity: 8,936,080 + 4,847,841 - 5,340,123 + 567,218 = 9,011,016. Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses, and Changes in Net Position (p11), which ties to the Statement of Activities business-type column (p3); measure net position; 18,352,565 + 13,380,175 - 10,699,816 - 567,218 = 20,465,706. Proprietary 'Other' 261,083 is charges for services because the Statement of Activities counts it in Charges for Services. 'Other grants' 358,503: no grantor printed, kept as category other with review (FY2023 used state aid without page evidence). Capital outlay 362,934: no function printed, labelled plain 'Capital Outlay'. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position - Modified Cash Basis (pp1-2), since the governmental funds statement (9,011,015) does not equal the government-wide governmental figures (capital assets, debt). Detail: the only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budgetary-basis comparison (p14), so detail is per fund column of the governmental funds statement (General, Debt Service, Community Redevelopment) and the single proprietary fund statement; p14 lines not recorded (as FY2023). Pages 15-16 are a second proprietary statement of revenues/expenses and cash flows (report pp53-54, no basis in title) with different figures (charges 12,613,972, net position 19,742,497 / 21,286,551); not used. Proprietary cash flow statement not recorded (proprietary null, as later years). Read pages 1-16 of 16"
}
